  "question": {
    "text": "An acidified solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Zn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is saturated with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>. What is the minimum molar concentration <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>)</mo></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math> required to prevent the precipitation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ZnS</mi></math>? Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi>sp</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>ZnS</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>22</mn></mrow></msup></math> and&nbsp;overall dissociation constant of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi>NET</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>21</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
